    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕleuthĕrĭus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευθέριος</span> (Liberator), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the surname of a god</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Liber,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, p. 207</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕleuthĕrĭa</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>the festival of Jupiter Eleutherius</i>, <i>feast
				of liberty</i>, celebrated in honor of the victory at Plataea,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 1, 1, 29</span></i>.</div>
